{
  "_comment": [
    "The engine's own reflection prompts, at the commit its v0.2.0 tag points at.",
    "Vendored because no built distribution of skillopt contains them: the wheel",
    "and the sdist on PyPI ship zero non-Python files, and a build from the git",
    "tag ships none either -- the pyproject declares packages but no package-data.",
    "So `load_prompt` raises FileNotFoundError at the first optimisation step of",
    "any environment, and the engine cannot complete one step as published.",
    "These are copies, byte-for-byte, restored into the installed package before a",
    "run. Authoring replacements would have been a patch: the prompts ARE the",
    "reflection strategy, which is the thing under study.",
    "Do not re-pin to silence a mismatch -- find out what changed upstream first."
  ],
  "repo": "microsoft/SkillOpt",
  "tag": "v0.2.0",
  "commit": "e4ea6a6771e797ef820cdd8bfea64c57e0481065",
  "member_root": "skillopt/",
  "license": "MIT",
  "retrieved": "2026-08-27",
  "upstream_defect": {
    "what": "no built distribution carries the package's .md data files",
    "cause": "pyproject.toml declares [tool.setuptools.packages.find] and no package-data",
    "effect": "load_prompt raises FileNotFoundError on the first reflect of any env",
    "checked_against": [
      "wheel 0.2.0",
      "sdist 0.2.0",
      "build from tag v0.2.0"
    ]
  },
